1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,000
Welcome to Project Pulse — a modern, real-time collaborative
project management platform built for fast-moving teams.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:14,500
Managing tasks across spreadsheets and scattered chats
slows teams down.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,000
Project Pulse brings planning, task tracking, live collaboration,
and analytics together in one clean workspace.

4
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,500
Starting from the workspace hub, you get an immediate overview
of all your active projects and total task counts,

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:32,000
alongside your overall completion rate and any overdue items.

6
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:42,000
The collapsible sidebar keeps navigation effortless, letting you
jump between projects or collapse the rail for maximum focus.

7
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:50,000
Inside a project, everything is organized into three focused views:
the Kanban Board, the Analytics Dashboard, and Team Members.

8
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:58,000
The interactive Kanban board organizes work across
To Do, In Progress, and Done columns.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Teams can instantly search tasks by title or filter by
status, priority, and assignee.

10
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:12,000
Clicking any card opens the task detail modal, where teammates
can update details and discuss work in threaded comments,

11
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
and inspect the complete chronological activity history.

12
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:24,500
The Analytics Dashboard turns live project data into clear
visual insights — tracking completion progress,

13
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:30,000
status and priority distribution, per-member workload,
and recent team activity.

14
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:37,500
Let's walk through a real workflow. We'll create a new
high-priority task, assign it to a teammate, and set a due date.

15
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:44,000
Submitting the form validates the input on the server,
saves it to the database, and updates the board immediately.

16
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:51,000
Dragging the card from To Do to In Progress triggers an
optimistic UI update while persisting the change via the API

17
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:57,000
and broadcasting the move in real time over Socket.IO.

18
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:04,000
Teammates can comment directly on the task, and every change
is logged automatically in the activity feed.

19
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Meanwhile, role-based permissions ensure only project owners
can manage team membership or project settings.

20
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:18,000
Under the hood, Project Pulse is built with Next.js 15 App Router,
React 19, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS on the frontend,

21
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
paired with dnd-kit for drag-and-drop and Recharts
for live data visualization.

22
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:33,000
On the backend, Next.js API routes validate requests with Zod,
enforce role-based access with signed JWT cookies,

23
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:40,000
and persist data through Prisma ORM and SQLite — while
Socket.IO broadcasts updates to authorized project rooms.

24
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:46,500
With real-time collaboration, intuitive Kanban workflows,
role-based security, and live analytics,

25
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:52,000
Project Pulse helps teams stay aligned from kickoff to launch.

26
00:02:52,500 --> 00:03:00,000
Thank you for watching this demonstration of Project Pulse.
